@inherits LocalizedComponent
@inject IJSRuntime JS

@*
    The playground's counterpart to the site's BrandHeading.astro: the mark, the product name
    as this app's one <h1>, and the tagline — same copy, same tokens, same geometry, so the two
    halves of the product read as one.

    THE MARK IS MEASURED HERE TOO, and it did not use to be. This component laid the heading out
    as a flex row and sized the mark to `1cap`, which is a normal-looking lockup and the wrong
    one: the site measures the `J` beside it and draws the mark from the cap line to the bottom
    of that letter's tail, which comes out about a quarter larger. At the sizes this page
    actually renders that was a 52-pixel mark on /why-justdummies against a 40-pixel one here,
    sitting at a different height inside the same heading. So the markup is the site's markup —
    an inline image in the heading's own text flow, aligned by `js/brand-heading.js`, which is
    the site's script with the same fallback behind it (see the file, and BrandHeading.astro).

    `data-brand-heading` is what that script finds the heading by, and it is the same attribute
    the site's brand carries — so tests/browser/chrome-parity.spec.ts can measure one against
    the other without either side knowing it is being compared.
*@

<div class="brand-heading">
    <h1 data-brand-heading>
        <img class="mark" src="/favicon-64.png" srcset="/favicon-64.png 2x, /favicon-128.png 4x" alt="" width="64" height="64" decoding="async" />JustDummies
    </h1>
    <p class="tagline">@PlaygroundStrings.T(LocaleState.Current, "brand.tagline")</p>
</div>

@code {

    /// <summary>
    ///     Aligns the mark against the heading it sits in, once the heading is in the document.
    ///
    ///     Only on the first render: the script installs its own resize and font listeners and
    ///     re-measures from there, so a language switch — which redraws this component without
    ///     changing a thing about the lockup — must not queue another interop call for it.
    /// </summary>
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender) {
        if (firstRender) {
            await JS.InvokeVoidAsync("jdBrandHeadingAlign");
        }
    }

}
